# fork/verify/known-failing-upstream — tests that already fail at the base tag.
#
# A DIFFERENT list from `known-failing`, with a different meaning and a different
# maintenance rule. `known-failing` records tests the FORK's seams turn red, and
# every entry there must pass at the base tag. This file records the opposite:
# tests that fail on upstream's own tree, at upstream's own release tag, before
# ore changes anything.
#
# They exist because upstream records its snapshots against `main`, where
# `[workspace.package] version` is 0.0.0, and cuts release tags as off-main
# commits that set the real version. Every status card and update-available
# snapshot therefore differs by that one string at any `rust-v*` tag. The rest
# are TLS-fallback, stack-depth and network-dependent tests that fail the same
# way on both sides.
#
# Every entry below was verified by running that exact test against the base tag
# in a clean worktree and observing it fail there too. Nothing goes in this file
# on suspicion -- if a test fails only on delta, it belongs in `known-failing`
# with a cause, or it is a bug.
#
# Re-derive after a sync: run the suite at the new base tag and diff.


